        82.6147232055664
      ],
      "text": "Extrapulmonary TB and TB meningitis",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        89.82263946533203,
        527.179443359375,
        104.26564025878906
      ],
      "text": "The WHO recommendations on longer MDR-TB regimens apply also to patients with extrapulmonary",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.976174354553223,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        103.02259063720703,
        527.3926391601562,
        117.46559143066406
      ],
      "text": "disease. Adjustments may be required, depending on the specific location of the disease. Treatment",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        116.22272491455078,
        527.226318359375,
        130.6657257080078
      ],
      "text": "of MDR/RR-TB meningitis is best guided by DST of the infecting strain and by knowledge of the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        129.42274475097656,
        527.5557250976562,
        143.86573791503906
      ],
      "text": "properties of TB medicines that cross the blood–brain barrier. Levofloxacin and moxifloxacin penetrate",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.972014427185059,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        141.34669494628906,
        527.5241088867188,
        157.06568908691406
      ],
      "text": "(83) the CNS well  , as do ethionamide or prothionamide, cycloserine or terizidone, linezolid and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        154.5467071533203,
        527.4324951171875,
        170.2657012939453
      ],
      "text": "(84, 85). imipenem–cilastatin   Seizures may be more common in children with meningitis treated with",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        169.02272033691406,
        527.3914184570312,
        183.46571350097656
      ],
      "text": "imipenem–cilastatin; thus, meropenem is preferred for meningitis cases and in children. High-dose",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        182.2227325439453,
        527.5933227539062,
        196.6657257080078
      ],
      "text": "isoniazid and pyrazinamide can also reach therapeutic levels in the cerebrospinal ﬂuid, and they may",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.997650146484375,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        194.14674377441406,
        527.4120483398438,
        209.86573791503906
      ],
      "text": "P be useful if the strains are susceptible.  -aminosalicylic acid and ethambutol do not penetrate the CNS",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.96679973602295,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        208.62269592285156,
        527.5636596679688,
        223.06568908691406
      ],
      "text": "well, and they should not be counted on as effective agents for MDR/RR-TB meningitis. Amikacin and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.983637809753418,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        221.8227081298828,
        527.4992065429688,
        236.2657012939453
      ],
      "text": "streptomycin penetrate the CNS only in the presence of meningeal inﬂammation. There are few data",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.99959945678711,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        233.74671936035156,
        527.4078979492188,
        249.46571350097656
      ],
      "text": "(86–88) on the CNS penetration of clofazimine, bedaquiline or delamanid  . In addition, cerebrospinal",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        248.2227325439453,
        424.4766540527344,
        262.6657409667969
      ],
      "text": "fluid concentrations may not mirror concentrations in the meninges or brain.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        279.06658935546875,
        127.81571197509766,
        294.7265930175781
      ],
      "text": "Pregnancy",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        301.93450927734375,
        527.5658569335938,
        316.3775329589844
      ],
      "text": "Amikacin, streptomycin, prothionamide and ethionamide are usually contraindicated during pregnancy.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.94486141204834,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        315.134521484375,
        527.5928344726562,
        329.5775451660156
      ],
      "text": "Because of the potential for teratogenic effects from these medications, including the injectable agents,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.951794624328613,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        328.3345031738281,
        527.4376831054688,
        342.77752685546875
      ],
      "text": "Recommendation 3.17 is of limited relevance in this subgroup. Following the changes made in the",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        341.5345153808594,
        527.4453735351562,
        355.9775390625
      ],
      "text": "2018 guidelines update, these agents are expected to be used less frequently in longer regimens.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        354.7344970703125,
        527.6055297851562,
        369.1775207519531
      ],
      "text": "Knowledge about the safety of bedaquiline and delamanid in pregnancy and breastfeeding is sparse.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.991146087646484,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        367.93450927734375,
        527.3939819335938,
        382.3775329589844
      ],
      "text": "However, new evidence from an observational study in South Africa was presented to the GDG 2019;",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.993648529052734,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        379.8584899902344,
        527.3992309570312,
        395.5775146484375
      ],
      "text": "(61) it included information on 58 mothers who received bedaquiline during pregnancy  . The results of",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.980683326721191,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86609649658203,
        394.3345031738281,
        524.4077758789062,
        408.77752685546875
      ],
      "text": "this study indicated that fetal exposure to bedaquiline in utero was associated with low birth weight 47",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        407.5345153808594,
        527.4093017578125,
        421.9775390625
      ],
      "text": "(45% of babies exposed to bedaquiline had a low birth weight compared with 26% of babies not",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        419.45849609375,
        527.3024291992188,
        435.1775207519531
      ],
      "text": "P (61) exposed,  =0.034)  . However, there were no other significant differences in infant outcomes,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        433.93450927734375,
        527.55419921875,
        448.3775329589844
      ],
      "text": "pregnancy outcomes or maternal treatment outcomes, including weight gain in the infants until",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        445.8584899902344,
        527.5546264648438,
        461.5775146484375
      ],
      "text": "(61) 1 year of age  . In such cases, it is recommended that a longer regimen be individualized to include",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 10.976725578308105,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        460.3345031738281,
        527.2484741210938,
        474.77752685546875
      ],
      "text": "components with a better established safety profile. The outcomes of treatment and pregnancy,",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        473.5345153808594,
        527.40478515625,
        487.9775390625
      ],
      "text": "including data from postpartum surveillance for congenital anomalies, should be documented to",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        486.7344970703125,
        430.765380859375,
        501.1775207519531
      ],
      "text": "help inform future recommendations for MDR-TB treatment during pregnancy.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        517.5784301757812,
        142.0622100830078,
        533.2384643554688
      ],
      "text": "HIV infection",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        540.4462890625,
        527.538330078125,
        554.8892822265625
      ],
      "text": "The composition of the treatment regimen for MDR-TB does not usually differ substantially for PLHIV.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.990546226501465,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        553.6463012695312,
        527.4191284179688,
        568.0892944335938
      ],
      "text": "With careful attention, it is possible to avoid certain drug–drug interactions (e.g. bedaquiline and",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        565.5703125,
        472.6365966796875,
        581.289306640625
      ],
      "text": "(44) efavirenz; see also the HIV drug interactions website of the University of Liverpool ).",
      "font": "SegoeUI-LightItalic",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        597.690185546875,
        317.9281921386719,
        613.3502197265625
      ],
      "text": "Patients with extensive pulmonary TB disease",
      "font": "SegoeUI-SemiBold",
      "size": 12.0,
      "type": "heading"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        620.5582275390625,
        527.5634765625,
        635.001220703125
      ],
      "text": "The duration of treatment post culture conversion may be modified according to the patient’s response",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.950187683105469,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        633.7581176757812,
        527.47509765625,
        648.2011108398438
      ],
      "text": "to therapy  (e.g. culture conversion before 2 months of treatment) and other risk factors for treatment  48",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 10.965997695922852,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        646.9581298828125,
        443.0183410644531,
        661.401123046875
      ],
      "text": "failure or relapse. This should be considered in patients with extensive TB disease.",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 11.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        699.037109375,
        249.56137084960938,
        712.7410888671875
      ],
      "text": "Low birth weight was defined as less than 2500 g.  47",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        70.86620330810547,
        711.4718017578125,
        526.566650390625,
        725.17578125
      ],
      "text": "“Bacteriological response” refers to bacteriological conversion with no reversion; “bacteriological conversion” describes a situation in a  48",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86620330810547,
        724.2718505859375,
        526.6119995117188,
        734.7758178710938
      ],
      "text": "patient with bacteriologically confirmed TB where at least two consecutive cultures (for DR-TB and drug-susceptible TB) or smears (for",
      "font": "SegoeUI-Light",
      "size": 8.0,
      "type": "paragraph"
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        81.86620330810547,
        733.871826171875,
        526.5777587890625,
        744.3757934570312
      ],
      "text": "drug-susceptible TB only), taken on different occasions at least 7 days apart, are negative; and “bacteriological reversion” describes a",
